From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 06:19:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: exynos9820-beyond2lte: Add the ramoops
 region

Bringing a secondary CPU online wedges this phone hard: the write to
/sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu1/online never returns, the USB link goes down
in the same second and the machine has to be forced off by holding the
buttons.  Measured on 22 September 2026 on kernel #39, which already
carries the CPU interrupt generator this port added for that call.

The problem is not that it hangs, it is that it hangs without a word.  The
kernel ring buffer dies with the machine, there is no serial console on
this board and the USB gadget that carries the log goes down with the hang
too, so every attempt costs one manual flash and yields nothing.

The vendor solves this with its own debug snapshot: a region of DRAM the
firmware does not clear across a warm reset.  This phone is known to keep
it, because the vendor kernel left an oops in it that this port read back
from /sys/fs/pstore after a reboot.  Take the same region, at the address
and size the vendor reserves for "debug-snapshot,log_kernel", and give it
to ramoops with a console buffer, so the last lines before a hang are
still there after the phone comes back.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts | 20 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
index 457a133006a..df360473eac 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos9820-beyond2lte.dts
@@ -207,6 +207,26 @@ cp_ram_logging@fb900000 {
 			no-map;
 		};
 
+		/*
+		 * A kernel log that survives a reset.  The vendor reserves this
+		 * region for "debug-snapshot,log_kernel" and its kernel keeps a
+		 * ramoops buffer in it, so this memory is known to outlive a warm
+		 * reset on this phone: the oops this port read back from
+		 * /sys/fs/pstore after a reboot came from here.
+		 *
+		 * Without it a hang leaves nothing behind.  Bringing a secondary
+		 * CPU online wedges this phone hard enough to take the USB link
+		 * with it, and the console buffer below is the only way to see
+		 * what the kernel printed last.
+		 */
+		ramoops@fd910000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
+			reg = <0x0 0xfd910000 0x200000>;
+			console-size = <0x100000>;
+			record-size = <0x20000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x20000>;
+		};
+
 		el2_earlymem@9fd800000 {
 			reg = <0x9 0xfd800000 0x2800000>;
 			no-map;
